    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d433">

                <pb facs="0580" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg566"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.24/6–1945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">La Paz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-19T16:00:00-04:00">June 19, 1945—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 20—12:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>641. Col. Doleman<anchor n="14" xml:id="d433-f1"/> states his opinion requested
                    by Minister National Defense with respect manner the four C—47 military planes
                    recently allocated this Govt, under Lend-Lease agreement may be utilized for
                    accomplishment Govt.’s program transport beef from lowlands to La Paz market.
                    Issues involved this plan concern opposition to it as commercial project on part
                    of Panagra<anchor n="15" xml:id="d433-f2"/> protégé Lloyd Aereo Boliviano, and
                    general propriety of so employing lend-lease equipment.</p>
                <p>In view obvious implications situation Col. Doleman intends bring matter
                    attention General Brett at Panama. I should be glad receive instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d433-f1" n="14" xml:id="d433-f1-content">
                <p>Col. Edgar C. Doleman, Chief of United States Military Mission in Bolivia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d433-f2" n="15" xml:id="d433-f2-content">
                <p>Pan American Grace Airways.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
